		{
			"id": "views-luminance",
			"kind": "scene",
			"shows": "The same scene in the Luminance view: each pixel painted with the color of its EV100 band",
			"caption": "Most of the floor falls in one yellow band, EV100 14 to 15. The cube reaches the top band, 16 and above. The shadows drop to green, 11 to 12: three steps, 8 times darker than the floor. Equal colors mean equal luminance.",
			"numbers": "Bands one EV wide from EV100 5 (SceneRenderer.h, LuminanceFirstEV100), twelve colors, the last from 16 on. The capture's lighting statistics: surfaces' EV100 p05 14.75, p50 14.88, p95 16.03, background median 15.63, so the floor (most surface pixels) is band 9 (14 to 15), the ground and sky beyond band 10, the cube band 11. The picture has seven flat colors; on the smoothly shaded sphere they touch in the order yellow-green, yellow, floor yellow, pale, white, so they are consecutive bands 5 to 11: teal 10 to 11, green 11 to 12. Floor to shadow: 3 bands, 2^3 = 8.",
			"alt": "The scene in flat color bands: a yellow floor, a near-white cube, green shadows with a blue-green core under the sphere, and bands of yellow and pale across the sphere and the sky.",
